      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Human herpevirus 8 (HHV8) has been localized to the endothelial and spindle cells of KS, suggesting a role for HHV8 in atherosclerosis. None of the 38 coronary atherectomy specimens contained HHV8 with both sensitive nested PCR assays, making it unlikely that persistent viral infection with HHV8 plays a role in coronary atherogenesis in the general population of the United States."},
